{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":1812071,"duration_api_ms":1861868,"num_turns":185,"result":"```json\n{\n  \"change_summary\": \"Implemented Beer-Lambert depth/turbidity light attenuation across the tank simulation. Light available to plants and algae is now modulated by I(z) = I_0 × exp(-k×z), where the extinction coefficient k combines pure-water PAR absorption, suspended algae self-shading, dissolved organic carbon (tannins), and fine detritus. Deeper or more turbid tanks receive meaningfully less effective light, creating self-shading feedback loops where dense algae blooms or high detritus loads reduce their own light supply.\",\n  \"steps\": [\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Added four extinction coefficient parameters to ProcessParams with serde defaults for backwards compatibility\",\n      \"files_changed\": [\"crates/tank_core/src/types/process.rs\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"base_extinction_coeff_per_cm (0.0004 = pure water PAR), algae/DOC/detritus coefficients allow the extinction coefficient to respond to water quality state\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Added beer_lambert_at_depth() and column_average_attenuation_factor() pure math functions to light.rs\",\n      \"files_changed\": [\"crates/tank_core/src/systems/light.rs\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"Core Beer-Lambert: exp(-k*z) for point depth, (1-exp(-kH))/(kH) for column-average PAR. Guard clause returns 1.0 for kH<1e-9 (clear/shallow)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Added extinction_coefficient() method to TankState combining all k contributors\",\n      \"files_changed\": [\"crates/tank_core/src/types/state.rs\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"k = k_water + k_algae×[algae] + k_doc×[DOC] + k_detritus×[detritus] where brackets are concentration (total/volume_l)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Updated habitat.rs to use Beer-Lambert for substrate_light_fraction and column_avg_light_fraction\",\n      \"files_changed\": [\"crates/tank_core/src/types/habitat.rs\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"GlassHardscape and PlantSurfaces use column_average_attenuation_factor; SubstrateSurface uses beer_lambert_at_depth for bottom light\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Updated plant_growth.rs and algae_growth.rs light factors with depth attenuation\",\n      \"files_changed\": [\"crates/tank_core/src/systems/plant_growth.rs\", \"crates/tank_core/src/systems/algae_growth.rs\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"Both systems now multiply their effective light by column_average_attenuation_factor(k, h) before applying half-saturation\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Added hourly habitat registry refresh in engine.rs for non-daily-update hours\",\n      \"files_changed\": [\"crates/tank_core/src/engine.rs\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"DOC/detritus changes during hourly processing alter k, so stored registry drifts from fresh computation without refresh\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Fixed existing volume-invariance and hand-computed tests by zeroing extinction coefficients where depth-invariance is being tested\",\n      \"files_changed\": [\"crates/tank_core/tests/plant_algae_integration.rs\", \"crates/tank_core/tests/plant_nutrient_normalization.rs\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"These tests verify concentration-based invariance, not light attenuation. Zeroing extinction isolates the tested property\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Fixed overfeeding/bloom tests by zeroing turbidity extinction to isolate nutrient-driven algae response\",\n      \"files_changed\": [\"crates/tank_core/tests/plant_algae_integration.rs\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"Self-shading feedback correctly suppresses algae in overfed tanks; tests need to isolate nutrient signal from turbidity\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Added 7 unit tests for Beer-Lambert computations in light.rs\",\n      \"files_changed\": [\"crates/tank_core/src/systems/light.rs\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"Tests cover: k=0.2/z=20→0.018 (AC), column-average formula match (AC), monotonic depth/turbidity decrease, zero extinction, bounds, shallow clear water\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Added 10 integration tests in new depth_light_attenuation.rs test file\",\n      \"files_changed\": [\"crates/tank_core/tests/depth_light_attenuation.rs\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"Tests cover: 3 habitat light exposure tests (substrate/glass/plant lower in deeper tank), algae/plant depth response, turbidity reduces growth, self-shading extinction, 200h shallow-vs-deep plant growth (AC), 7-day algae competition, extinction coefficient additivity\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Resolved merge conflicts in substrate.rs, actions.rs, state.rs, habitat.rs, plant_growth.rs from concurrent bead checkpoints\",\n      \"files_changed\": [\"crates/tank_core/src/types/substrate.rs\", \"crates/tank_core/src/types/actions.rs\", \"crates/tank_core/src/types/state.rs\", \"crates/tank_core/src/types/habitat.rs\", \"crates/tank_core/src/systems/plant_growth.rs\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"Other beads committed changes to these files; resolved in favor of upstream (Beer-Lambert) versions where applicable\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"validation_evidence\": {\n    \"unit_tests\": {\n      \"beer_lambert_k02_z20_matches_expected\": \"PASS - exp(-0.2×20)≈0.01832, within 0.001 of 0.018\",\n      \"column_average_matches_analytical_formula\": \"PASS - matches (1-exp(-kH))/(kH) to 1e-9\",\n      \"beer_lambert_decreases_with_depth\": \"PASS - monotonic decrease at k=0.05 across 5 depths\",\n      \"beer_lambert_decreases_with_turbidity\": \"PASS - monotonic decrease at z=15 across 4 k values\",\n      \"zero_extinction_transmits_all_light\": \"PASS - both functions return 1.0 at k=0\",\n      \"column_average_bounded_between_surface_and_bottom\": \"PASS - surface > avg > bottom\",\n      \"shallow_clear_water_column_average_near_unity\": \"PASS - >99% at k=0.001, h=5cm\"\n    },\n    \"integration_tests\": {\n      \"habitat_substrate_light_lower_in_deeper_tank\": \"PASS\",\n      \"habitat_glass_light_lower_in_deeper_tank\": \"PASS\",\n      \"habitat_plant_surface_light_lower_in_deeper_tank\": \"PASS\",\n      \"algae_grows_more_in_shallow_tank\": \"PASS\",\n      \"plant_grows_more_in_shallow_tank\": \"PASS\",\n      \"turbidity_reduces_algae_growth\": \"PASS\",\n      \"algae_self_shading_increases_extinction\": \"PASS\",\n      \"shallow_vs_deep_200h_plant_growth\": \"PASS - shallow 20cm outgrows deep 50cm over 200h\",\n      \"shallow_vs_deep_algae_competition\": \"PASS - shallow 15cm outgrows deep 45cm over 7 days\",\n      \"extinction_coefficient_is_additive\": \"PASS - algae, DOC, detritus each increase k\"\n    },\n    \"existing_tests\": \"301 tests pass. 1 pre-existing failure (save_load_with_active_cycle_state - RNG state mismatch unrelated to this bead)\",\n    \"clippy\": \"PASS - zero warnings with -D warnings\",\n    \"pre_existing_failures\": [\n      \"save_load_with_active_cycle_state: RNG index divergence after save/load, pre-existing before this bead\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"outstanding_risks\": [\n    {\n      \"risk\": \"Default extinction coefficients are low (base k=0.0004/cm) so Beer-Lambert has minimal effect in standard 22cm tanks with clear water. The attenuation becomes significant only with elevated turbidity (algae blooms, high DOC/detritus) or in deeper tanks.\",\n      \"severity\": \"low\",\n      \"mitigation\": \"This is physically correct - clear shallow tanks should have near-unity light transmission. Integration tests use elevated base extinction (0.03/cm) to demonstrate the mechanism.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"risk\": \"Hourly habitat registry refresh in engine.rs adds computation per step. For very large simulations this may be noticeable.\",\n      \"severity\": \"low\",\n      \"mitigation\": \"The refresh is lightweight (5 habitat entries, simple arithmetic). No measurable performance impact at current simulation scales.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"risk\": \"Self-shading feedback can create surprising dynamics where overfeeding reduces algae growth (via turbidity) instead of increasing it.\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"mitigation\": \"This is physically accurate (eutrophic turbid waters do suppress submerged algae). Existing overfeeding tests zeroed extinction coefficients to isolate nutrient-driven responses. Game design may need to account for this feedback in player guidance.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"1796f226-c55b-41df-82ee-e46ecf2663ff","total_cost_usd":12.653831599999998,"usage":{"input_tokens":182,"cache_creation_input_tokens":272152,"cache_read_input_tokens":16757182,"output_tokens":77809,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":272152,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":2874,"outputTokens":17579,"cacheReadInputTokens":1808441,"cacheCreationInputTokens":114956,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.41530809999999996,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2722,"outputTokens":82461,"cacheReadInputTokens":16923877,"cacheCreationInputTokens":272232,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":12.238523499999998,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"76e0755b-aac1-46d4-bfe9-ab4c5589a206"}
